  "unit": "u02-pronouns",
  "title": "Where are you from?",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "**আপনি কোথা থেকে এসেছেন?** (*apni kotha theke eshechhen?*) — literally 'You from where have come?' — is how you ask 'Where are you from?'. Answer: **আমি আমেরিকা থেকে এসেছি** 'I have come from America.'\n\nTwo things to notice:\n\n- **থেকে** 'from' comes **after** the place: বাংলাদেশ থেকে = 'from Bangladesh'. Bengali has *post*positions, not prepositions.\n- **কোথায়** 'where' shortens to **কোথা** before থেকে.\n\nLearn **এসেছি / এসেছেন** as chunks for now; the past tense comes in Unit 9.\n\nCulture: a very common Bangladeshi icebreaker is **আপনার দেশ কোথায়?** or **আপনার বাড়ি কোথায়?** — 'Where is your home?' It usually means *which district is your family from*, even if you live in Dhaka.",
  "vocab": [
